  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}}$ be the $\\mathrm{n}^{\\text {th }}$ term of an A. P.<br/>If $S_n=a_1+a_2+a_3+\\ldots+a_n=700, a_6=7$ and $S_7=7$, then $\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}}$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "utPe3",
      "text": "56",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pOflJ",
      "text": "65",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "B8eii",
      "text": "64",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "5JUF7",
      "text": "70",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{n}}=700=\\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{2}[2 \\mathrm{a}+(\\mathrm{n}-1) \\mathrm{d}]$...(i)<br/>$a_6=7 \\Rightarrow a+5 d=7$...(ii)<br/>$\\mathrm{S}_7=7 \\Rightarrow \\frac{7}{2}(2 \\mathrm{a}+6 \\mathrm{~d})=7$<br/>$a+3 d=1$...(iii)<br/>Solve (ii) and (iii)<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{2}(-16+3 n-3)=700 \\Rightarrow 3 n^2-19 n-1400=0 \\\\\n& (3 n+56)(\\mathrm{n}-25)=0 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{a}_{25}=\\mathrm{a}+24 \\mathrm{~d}=-8+24 \\times 3 \\\\\n& =-8+72<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>=64",
    "image": null
  },
